==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{G.}} ''[[Autismus]]'', coined 1912 by Swiss psychiatrist [[w:Paul Bleuler|Paul Bleuler]] (1857-1939) from {{Gr.}} '''[[αυτός]]''' (autos-) "self" (comb. form) + '''[[-ισμός]]''' (-ismos) suffix "of action" or "of state".

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{clinical psychology}} Abnormal [[self-absorption]], first observed in [[childhood]], characterised by lack of [[response]] to people and limited ability to [[communicate]].

